<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian 91-day T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian 91-day T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills fell to 10.250 percent from 10.257 percent at the previous auction on August 28.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Dec 5, 1996 (Nov 28, 1996)</p>
<p>Average yield: 10.250 percent (10.257)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 810.550 million (925.725 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 910.550 million (976.425 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 10.002-10.285 percent (10.002-10.285)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 10.002-10.500 percent (10.002-10.500)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 151 (152)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 155 (168)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.40 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
